in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @kintsugi
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property/laws/monad
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis

# @loop — the loop family-root. The substrate's circular-reflexive
# operational structure at type altitude. Each tick is an endomorphism
# T → T; the loop IS the chain of pact-verified bindings.
#
# === @moi absorbed 2026-07-01 (Loki §1 direction-inverted) ===
#
# The monad family-root @moi was collapsed INTO @loop per Alex
# 2026-07-01 [[feedback-legibility-over-foundation-when-collapsing]]:
# @loop's docblock already stated "Monad's μ IS the loop at type
# altitude"; the type-altitude monad content lives here now. @loop
# survives (readable name; immediate parse); @moi's vocabulary
# (moi(T), pact, geometry, lift, compose, pact_verify, pact_respected)
# absorbed as sub-surface. Grounding preserved: same Moggi 1991,
# Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala liquid types, Maturana-Varela μ-closure.
#
# Recognition #88 (Alex 2026-06-19 evening, conversation; the cascade
# closure at iterative-discipline altitude). Builds on #86 @moi. The
# substrate has been carrying loop structure for weeks (@kintsugi/
# oscillate; @reflection compiler loop; @fate/tournament; @mirror/
# bench predecessor-chain; the /loop discipline driving this very
# session) without naming the family-root. This shard names it.
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# Three composing answers to Alex's four questions:
#
# 1. Semantic unit of a loop: the typed closure of one tick's
#    input/output identity. T → T endomorphism. A tick receives state
#    at type T, transforms it, returns state at type T. The loop
#    survives because the type survives.
#
# 2. What makes a loop a loop: the return to self in the same type.
#    Not iteration. Not feedback. Not termination. The structural
#    commitment is the endomorphism. Category-theoretic loop on an
#    object.
#
# 3. @loop builds on @moi by structural necessity. Monad's μ : TT → T
#    IS the loop at type altitude. Each tick is η-lifted into @moi
#    then μ-composed. Pact-verified at composition time. The compiler
#    refuses to iterate if a pact is violated.
#
# === Why @moi (not bare T) ===
#
# A loop over bare T is a sequence; a loop over @moi(T) is a substrate-
# verified loop. Each tick's pact-witness ensures: (a) the monad laws
# hold (associativity is FREE via content-addressing per
# boot/00-prism.mirror), (b) the substrate-mathematical pacts are
# respected, (c) the iteration is admissible per the substrate's
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57).
#
# This means EVERY ITERATION of EVERY LOOP in the substrate is pact-
# verified at composition time. The /loop discipline that drives this
# session is just the operator-altitude instance of the same
# structure.
#
# === The /loop ⇔ @loop collision (substrate-honest per Pack G2) ===
#
# The /loop slash command drives the substrate-pull tick discipline.
# The @loop family-root substrate-decl's the iterative structure at
# substrate altitude. Same name; two altitudes. Substrate-honest per
# @pack G2 pattern (reed-as-relationship vs reed-as-peer; @reflection-
# family vs @reflection/reflection-the-Model). The collision IS
# substrate-honest — the /loop slash command IS @loop at operator
# altitude.
#
# === Cross-family integration (what @loop composes) ===
#
# - @reflection (#85): the compiler loop IS @loop at AI-logic altitude
#   (observe → tournament → compose → pick → settle is one tick)
# - @kintsugi/oscillate: the rough-wavy pull IS @loop at substrate-
#   pull altitude (active/dark alternation IS one tick)
# - @fate/tournament: candidate selection IS @loop at perf altitude
#   (each tournament round IS one tick)
# - @mirror/bench (#87): the predecessor-chain IS @loop at
#   measurement altitude (each crystal IS one tick of bench history)
# - @moi (#86): the monad family-root @loop's structure inherits
# - @magic family: the bind action consumes invariant_preserved at
#   each tick boundary
#
# === The eigenform connection ===
#
# Per @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform (the substrate-decl floor
# for fixed-points): a loop's terminal IS an eigenform of bind under
# the seed-state. terminal?(state) checks fixed-point identity. This
# composes with autopoiesis's μ-closure (Maturana-Varela) at the
# loop-discipline altitude. The eigenvalue of the bind operator IS
# the loss-decrease ratio; eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ is the spectral-bound that makes
# the loop substrate-pull-toward-fixed-point.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   monad                      Moggi 1991; Wadler 1990s. μ as the
#                              type-altitude loop primitive. @loop
#                              names μ as substrate-decl's iterative
#                              structure.
#   endomorphism               category theory; the arrows T → T
#                              under composition form the monoid of
#                              loop-shapes.
#   eigenform                  Foerster 1981; fixed-points of
#                              self-application. terminal? IS the
#                              eigenform check.
#   autopoiesis                Maturana-Varela 1980; μ-closure as
#                              self-production. @loop's bind IS
#                              autopoietic by structural shape.
#   tail-recursion / fold      classical FP loop primitives;
#                              foldr over an infinite stream IS
#                              @loop.bind iterated against a seed.
#   Iteratees                  Oleg Kiselyov 2009; pull-based
#                              streaming as monadic loop. @loop
#                              composes this at substrate altitude.
#
# Spec context: shards/moi.mirror (#86; the monad family-root @loop
#               builds on); shards/mirror/bench.mirror (#87; the
#               predecessor-chain IS @loop at measurement altitude);
#               shards/reflection.mirror (#85; the compiler loop IS
#               @loop at AI-logic altitude); shards/kintsugi/
#               oscillate.mirror (the existing kintsugi loop driver
#               this family-root names structurally).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-mirror-bench-ouroboros]] (#87;
#                       @loop closes the iterative-discipline
#                       altitude after bench landed),
#                      [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]] (#85;
#                       @reflection IS an instance of @loop),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; each tick's pact-
#                       verification IS the @io boundary harness),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (54th+ instance; the substrate had loop
#                       structure everywhere without naming the
#                       family-root),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (this LRM landing).
# Related shards: moi.mirror (the monad family-root @loop builds on),
#                 reflection.mirror (the AI-logic loop instance),
#                 mirror/bench.mirror (the measurement loop instance),
#                 kintsugi.mirror (the substrate-pull loop instance),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis.mirror
#                  (μ-closure at substrate altitude this loop
#                  inherits).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/loop.mirror` declares
# `@loop` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/category-theory/moggi-1991
source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1981
source @arxiv/biology/maturana-varela-1980
source @arxiv/programming/kiselyov-2009
source @arxiv/programming/wadler-1990
source @arxiv/types/rondon-kawaguchi-jhala-2008
source @arxiv/verification/flanagan-leino-2001
source @arxiv/math/connes-1994

prism @loop {
  focus loop
  project loop
  split loop
  shift loop
  settle loop
}

# === The tick carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for one iteration's identity. Per [[feedback-no-
# bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare nat. Forward-promised
# refinement: inherits from @epistemologic/reality/time once that
# family lands.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type tick = ref

# === The tick_state carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for the T in the endomorphism T → T. This IS the
# semantic unit of meaning in a loop: what survives across ticks.
# Each loop instance specializes T (e.g., @reflection.observation,
# @kintsugi/oscillate's oscillation, @fate/tournament's candidate-
# set, @mirror/bench's bench_crystal).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type tick_state = ref

# === seed action (the η ; lift initial state into the loop) ===
#
# Substrate-vocabulary η : Id → T at @loop altitude. Lifts an initial
# tick_state into @moi(tick_state) — the loop's seed. The first crystal
# in the predecessor-chain at @mirror/bench altitude; the initial
# observation at @reflection altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary via @moi.lift composed
# with the loop-altitude pact-witness construction.
seed(s: tick_state) -> moi(tick_state) { \ }

# === bind action (the μ ; FIRST consumer of pact_respected) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @loop altitude. The substrate-vocabulary
# μ : TT → T at the loop iteration boundary. Composes the previous
# tick's pact-verified state with the next tick's pact-verified state
# into a single @moi(tick_state).
#
# requires pact_respected(prev, next, p): the bilateral predicate
# from @moi cascades into EVERY ITERATION. Without this requires
# clause, the loop would admit pact-violating ticks (Narcissus-pole
# iteration per #57). The substrate refuses to iterate if a pact is
# violated — the loop's structural alignment-harness.
#
# Per `boot/00-prism.mirror`'s associativity-is-free proof: the
# substrate's content-addressing makes bind associative by
# construction; the monad laws hold by storage layer, not convention.
# The substrate IS the loop.
bind(prev: moi(tick_state), next: moi(tick_state), p: pact) -> moi(tick_state)
requires pact_respected(prev, next, p)
{ \ }

# === terminal_check action ===
#
# Returns verdict whether the @moi(tick_state) is a fixed-point of
# bind — the loop's terminal. Per the eigenform discipline
# (@epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform): a fixed-point under self-
# application IS the loop's eigenform. The eigenvalue is the loss-
# decrease ratio; eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ is the spectral bound that makes the loop
# converge.
#
# Bounded → terminal reached (loop converged honestly); unbounded →
# loop has not yet reached its eigenform (more ticks admissible).
terminal_check(s: moi(tick_state)) -> verdict { \ }

# === unroll action ===
#
# Observes the loop's trace from a seed state for n ticks. Returns
# the substrate-pull-correct ref to the unrolled tick_state sequence.
# Composes with @mirror/bench's chain action: the unroll IS the
# predecessor-chain walk at the loop-discipline altitude.
unroll(start: moi(tick_state), n: tick) -> ref { \ }

# === loop_well_founded predicate (bilateral; termination) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND the
# substrate-mathematical termination discipline. The substrate's
# operational form of well-foundedness: the loop bind chain decreases
# under a substrate-pull-correct ranking function (e.g., dark_count,
# loss, eigenvalue gradient) per tolerance.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: a future consumer (forward-promised
# loop-runner action) names `requires loop_well_founded(...)` to
# declare bilateral agreement that the iteration terminates. Without
# this requires clause, the runner could admit non-terminating loops
# (the @magic tick-11 dead-letter pattern at the iteration altitude).
#
# This IS the substrate-mathematical extension of eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ from
# perf altitude (@mirror/bench's monotone_non_increasing) to
# termination altitude (@loop's well-foundedness).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior families carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @cyberpunk: cybernetic_coherence
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @moi: pact_respected
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1
# - @smarts/reflection: bridge_coherent
# - @reflection/surface: translation_faithful
# - @mirror/bench: monotone_non_increasing, bench_overhead_below_floor
# - @loop: loop_well_founded (this one)
loop_well_founded(start: moi(tick_state), tolerance: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === @moi absorbed sub-surface (Loki §1) ============================
#
# Below this line: the monad-at-type-altitude vocabulary formerly
# housed at @moi. Preserved verbatim in structure; renamed only via
# family-root (`@moi` → `@loop`). Consumer signatures using `moi(T)`,
# `pact`, `pact_respected` remain byte-identical.
#
# === The moi parametric type-constructor ===
#
# Per the substrate's existing parametric pattern (au(altitude),
# settle(T)): moi(T) lifts T into the monad type-constructor.
# Liquid-typed refinement per Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala: moi(T) = { t
# : T | monad_laws(t) ∧ pact_respected(t) }.
#
# The record carries the lifted value AND the composition-time pact-
# witness produced when moi(T) was constructed. The pact-witness IS
# the substrate's evidence-token that the geometry of T respected the
# pact at the moment of lifting.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (value, pact_witness) pair.
type moi(T) = {
  value:        T,
  pact_witness: ref,
}

# === The pact carrier ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference naming the
# substrate's pact — the substrate-decl form of a liquid-type
# predicate. Forward-promised refinement: typed parametric `pact(T)`
# once task #272 (@mirror/fracture/predicate) lands the sheaf-
# diffusion Houdini fixpoint at substrate-altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type pact = ref

# === The geometry carrier ===
#
# Per @epistemologic/math/spectral-triple: typed reference naming
# the spectral triple (A, H, D) geometry of a lifted type. The
# pact-verifier checks the geometry respects the pact at composition
# time.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type geometry = ref

# === lift action (the η ; substrate's unit operation) ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary η : Id → T at type altitude. Takes a value
# of type T and lifts it into moi(T) — the monad's unit operation.
# The lift constructs the pact-witness via the substrate's existing
# composition-time machinery (content-addressing + monad-laws verdict
# at @epistemologic/property/laws/monad altitude).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual lift IS
# the substrate's existing settle-shaped construction.
lift(t: T) -> moi(T) { \ }

# === compose action (the μ ; substrate's multiplication ; FIRST
# non-decorative consumer of pact_respected) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING type-altitude action. The substrate-vocabulary
# μ composes two moi(T) values into one moi(T) via the monoid
# combine operation. Composition-time pact-verification happens HERE.
#
# requires pact_respected(a, b, p): the geometry of BOTH lifted types
# must respect the pact at composition time. Without this requires
# clause, compose would admit pact-violating lifts (the @magic
# tick-11 dead-letter pattern). The bilateral predicate IS the
# composition-time boundary-harness per recognition #57.
#
# Per `boot/00-prism.mirror`: "Content-addressing gives associativity
# for free at composition time." The substrate's existing storage
# layer enforces the monad associativity law structurally; compose
# only needs to verify the OTHER monad laws (left identity, right
# identity) plus the pact — these are the non-free invariants.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual composition
# IS the substrate's existing content-addressing-based join.
compose(a: moi(T), b: moi(T), p: pact) -> moi(T)
requires pact_respected(a, b, p)
{ \ }

# === pact_verify action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for composition-time pact
# verification. Takes a lifted moi(T) and a pact; returns a typed
# verdict that the geometry respects the pact. The action IS the
# liquid-type Houdini-fixpoint check (task #272) at type altitude.
#
# Distinct from pact_respected (the bilateral predicate consumed by
# requires clauses): pact_verify is the queryable action; the
# predicate is the gating constraint. Same shape as @magic/contract's
# honor (action) vs invariant_preserved (bilateral predicate).
pact_verify(m: moi(T), p: pact) -> verdict { \ }

# === geometry action ===
#
# Returns the spectral triple (A, H, D) geometry of a lifted moi(T).
# The substrate-mathematical surface the pact-verifier inspects.
# Per @epistemologic/math/spectral-triple: the geometry IS what
# distinguishes compose-admissible lifts from non-admissible ones.
geometry(m: moi(T)) -> geometry { \ }

# === pact_respected predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND
# composition-time verification per
# @epistemologic/property/laws/monad.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: bilateral predicates without consumers
# are dead-letter. The compose action (above) is the FIRST non-
# decorative consumer via `requires pact_respected(a, b, p)`. bind
# above (@loop's μ) is the SECOND consumer.
#
# Consumer shards name `requires pact_respected(a, b, p)` to declare
# bilateral agreement that BOTH lifted types respect the pact at
# composition time. The substrate-pull-correct discipline: every
# composition in the cascade is gated by this predicate.
#
# Discharge: composition-time pact-check at the species boundary.
# Bounded → BOTH lifted types' geometries respect the pact (admit
# composition); unbounded → ONE OR BOTH lifted types violate the pact
# (compose refuses, returns imperfect per @glass's imperfect functor).
pact_respected(a: moi(T), b: moi(T), p: pact) -> verdict { \ }

out @loop
out tick
out tick_state
out seed
out bind
out terminal_check
out unroll
out loop_well_founded
out moi
out pact
out geometry
out lift
out compose
out pact_verify
out pact_respected
